        "condition": "Used",
        "price": 10000,
        "description": "<p><strong>Ferrari&nbsp;<a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Societ%C3%A0_per_Azioni\" title=\"Societ\u00e0 per Azioni\">S.p.A.</a></strong>&nbsp;(<a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Help:IPA/English\" title=\"Help:IPA/English\">/f\u0259\u02c8r\u0251\u02d0ri/</a>;&nbsp;<small>Italian:&nbsp;</small><a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Help:IPA/Italian\" title=\"Help:IPA/Italian\">[fer\u02c8ra\u02d0ri]</a>) is an&nbsp;<a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Italy\" title=\"Italy\">Italian</a>&nbsp;<a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Luxury_vehicle\" title=\"Luxury vehicle\">luxury</a>&nbsp;<a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sports_car\" title=\"Sports car\">sports car</a>&nbsp;<a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Manufacturer\" title=\"Manufacturer\">manufacturer</a>&nbsp;based in&nbsp;<a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Maranello\" title=\"Maranello\">Maranello</a>, Italy. Founded by&nbsp;<a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Enzo_Ferrari\" title=\"Enzo Ferrari\">Enzo Ferrari</a>&nbsp;in 1939 out of the&nbsp;<a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Alfa_Romeo\" title=\"Alfa Romeo\">Alfa Romeo</a>&nbsp;race division as&nbsp;<em>Auto Avio Costruzioni</em>, the company built&nbsp;<a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Auto_Avio_Costruzioni_815\" title=\"Auto Avio Costruzioni 815\">its first car</a>&nbsp;in 1940. However, the company&#39;s inception as an&nbsp;<a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Auto_manufacturer\" title=\"Auto manufacturer\">auto manufacturer</a>&nbsp;is usually recognized as 1947, when the first Ferrari-badged car was completed.</p>",
